 "audit": "Extreme burden heterogeneity: a few hypermutated cases (up to 15,731 mutations; median about 5) and pooled diagnosis labels (NOS, malignant glioma, missing/Unknown) mix entities, so Fisher tests are inflated for hypermutated diagnoses. Long genes (ARID1B, ZMYM3, ASXL1, KMT2D) with scattered missense and no hotspots look like passenger or burden effects; I down-weighted them. PIK3R1 in pilocytic astrocytoma is strong despite low burden but unexplained and not in the literature I know. No sex/site/age or batch adjustment; small diagnosis groups (n<15) give unstable frequencies. Multiple testing across ~2500 pairs.",
 "agent": "sonnet-neutral-T-r3"
